{
  "description": "core §2.7 (0.24), a population: a resource's `kind`, its `bound` (an integer, \"no_ceiling\" or \"untemplated\"), an event's `retention_s`, and one reading → whether the instance holds more live members than its bound (`expect.verdict`: exceeds, within, unobservable or not_asked) and the reason class (`expect.reason`). A reading is an owner's S4 GET of a state resource (`via: get`: how many keys it answered with a value, and whether it ran to its final reply) or a subscription window over a stream or an event (`via: window`: per member, the seconds at which it was heard, on one clock; `listened_s`, how long it listened; `lossless`, false when it lost a delivery; `present`, false when the owner was not present, an instance token held, from the window's start to its end). A window counts the most members heard within any span shorter than the liveness span, an hour for a stream and the retention for an event: two instants exactly one span apart are not within it. A window is complete when it listened at least one span, was lossless, and the owner was present throughout. Reasons are chosen in this order: not_asked (kind: an operation; no_ceiling; untemplated); unobservable reading_kind (a window of a state, a GET of a stream or an event); exceeds over_bound (in any reading); unobservable incomplete (a GET that did not run to its final reply), or, for a window, lossy, then window_too_short, then owner_absent; unobservable empty (no member, O5); within complete.",
